{
  "title": "TKA in Patella Baja (Prior HTO)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/recon/5018/tka-in-patella-baja-prior-hto",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jan 30 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "TKA in Patella Baja is characterized by performing a TKA in a patient with a prior high tibial osteotomy that caused lowering of the patella relative to its normal position.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made with plain radiographs of the knee showing an Insall-Salvati ratio of < 0.8.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment of patellar baja in a TKA involves various techniques including lowering the joint line, placing the patellar component superiorly, or performing a tibial tubercle transfer.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology of acquired patella baja",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common causes include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**proximal tibial osteotomy**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "patella baja is the most common complication seen following proximal tibial opening-wedge osteotomy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "may be caused by shortening of the patellar tendon during tibial osteotomy or from scarring of the patellar tendon post-operatively",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**tibial tubercle slide or transfer**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**trauma to the proximal tibia**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**technical error during primary total knee replacement (joint line elevation)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**ACL reconstruction**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**total knee arthroplasty**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "patella infera is an important consideration when performing total knee arthroplasty",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "improper technique may cause patella baja",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "special techniques must be utilized when performing TKA in patients with patella baja from congenital or acquired (tibial osteotomy, prior TKA) causes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "anterior impingement knee pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "knee stiffness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanical block to full flexion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**limited flexion due to patellar impingement** on the tibia in extremes of flexion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral views of the knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral view of the knee in 30 degrees of flexion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "used to measure **Insall-Salvati ratio**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "measures ratio patellar tendon length to patellar bone length",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [
                            {
                              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/5018/images/insallsal.do.jpg",
                              "caption": "shows Insall-Salvati ratio"
                            }
                          ],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "normal Insall-Salvati is 1:1 between length of the patellar tendon length to patellar bone length",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lateral view in extension",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "distal positioning of the patella in relation to the trochlear groove",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/5018/images/xr%20patella%20baja.jpg",
                          "caption": "Patella baja"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**Insall-Salvati ratio of < 0.8 is consistent with patella baja**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "activity modifications, physical therapy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "mild symptoms in younger patients",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "total knee replacement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "severe impingement in older patients with osteoarthritis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Total knee arthroplasty in patient with patella baja**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "methods to address patella infera during TKA",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**place patellar component superiorly**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "mild patella baja",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "technique",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "use a smaller patellar dome placed on superior aspect of patella",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "trim inferior bone to decrease flexion impingement",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**lower joint line**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "moderate patella baja",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "technique",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**add distal femoral augmentation**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**cut more proximal tibia to lower joint line (lower tibial cut)**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "avoid bone cuts that raise the joint line",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "raising the joint line will effectively increase the patella baja deformity",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "5",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "may require revision knee system",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**transfer tibial tubercle to cephalad position**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "moderate patella baja",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "technique",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "technique is difficult due to complexity of a tibial transfer in proximity to a cemented tibial component",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "outcomes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "unpredictable bone healing leads to variable, and often poor, outcomes",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "patients may be left with extensor lag",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**patellectomy**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**severe patella baja**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "techniques",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "alters the tension in the anterior knee mechanism",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "therefore recommended to use **use a cruciate substituting system**",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "5",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "consider partial patellectomy in which patella is resected to a width of 10-12mm.",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "lessens impingement & crepitus while maintaining some of the fulcrum of the patella.",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
